% Twin of Vault (contracts/Vault.sol: a collateral vault reading a price feed (the E12 worked example)), translated by the Solidity translator.
% One law per success path of each state-changing function, one integrity constraint per revert path;
% the reverts' reasons are the comments above the constraints. See vault.ledger.md;
% the contract itself: sources/Vault.sol (File > Show the Original in the Logical English editor, View > The original this was converted from in the LPS2 IDE).
% Who may do what, when, with which effect: the legal view, computed from this program
% (Misc > Legal View of This LPS Program in the Logical English editor, View > Legal view in the LPS2 IDE).
% Related: vault_oracle.le is this twin with the borrow residue below filled in by the E12 convention
% (the price feed as an event and a fluent) — a hand-written extension whose deposit laws are these, checked
% by test_solidity.pl; vault_view.le is its legal-readable view with the price as an assumable question.

the target language is: lps.

the maximum time is 4.

the actions are:
    *a caller* calls deposit with amount *an amount*; known as call_deposit.
    *a caller* calls borrow with amount *an amount*; known as call_borrow.

the fluents are:
    the feed of the contract is *an account*; known as feed; the zero address by default.
    the collateral of *an account* is *an amount*; known as collateral; 0 by default.
    the debt of *an account* is *an amount*; known as debt; 0 by default.

the constants are:
    the largest amount is 115792089237316195423570985008687907853269984665640564039457584007913129639935.

the knowledge base vault includes:

% deposit
% reverts: Panic 0x11 (arithmetic overflow or underflow)
it must not be true that
    a caller calls deposit with amount an amount
    and the collateral of the caller is a second amount
    and second amount + amount > the largest amount.

when a caller calls deposit with amount an amount
then the collateral of the caller that is a second amount becomes second amount + amount.

% borrow
% RESIDUE Vault_borrow BEGIN: paths of borrow through external_call
% TODO: translate the fragment below by hand, or with the Contract Assistant (residue mode); it was not translated automatically
%   source: function borrow, src 778:270:0
% The other paths of this function are translated below; these are for the assistant (residue mode) or a person.
%   solidity:
%   | function borrow(uint256 amount) external {
%   |         uint256 price = feed.latestPrice();
%   |         if (collateral[msg.sender] * price < 2 * (debt[msg.sender] + amount)) {
%   |             revert Undercollateralised(msg.sender);
%   |         }
%   |         debt[msg.sender] += amount;
%   |     }
% RESIDUE Vault_borrow END

